    "updated_at": "2022-03-08T04:15:23Z",
    "body": "For Blink's implementation, knowing whether something can throw is useful, because it changes the calling convention.\r\n\r\nHowever, in practice there's stuff that can throw in Blink that never throws in the spec, so we can't use the spec as the ultimate source of truth. For example, stack overflow and Worker termination can cause many V8 operations to throw.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
